{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "***early life***  \nRaymond III, Count of Tripoli, was born in the early 12th century, around 1130, into a prominent noble family of the Crusader states. He was the son of Raymond II, Count of Tripoli, and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His family was deeply rooted in the political and military affairs of the Levant, and his upbringing was shaped by the turbulent and often violent environment of the region.\n\n***reign as count of tripoli***  \nRaymond succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152, taking on the mantle of leadership at a crucial time in the history of the Crusader states. His reign was marked by a series of challenges, including the threat of Muslim invasions and internal power struggles. Despite these difficulties, Raymond managed to maintain the county's sovereignty and even expand its influence in some areas. He was known for his strategic acumen and military prowess, which were instrumental in defending the Crusader states against various enemies.\n\n***contributions and legacy***  \nRaymond III's contributions to the Crusader states were significant and far-reaching. He played a key role in the political and military affairs of the Levant, often acting as a mediator between different factions. His leadership was characterized by a focus on defense and consolidation, rather than aggressive expansion. Raymond's efforts helped stabilize the region and ensure the survival of the Crusader states for several decades. He is remembered as a capable and respected leader who navigated the complexities of the medieval Middle East with skill and determination.\n\n***conflict with the byzantine empire***  \nOne of the significant challenges faced by Raymond III was the conflict with the Byzantine Empire. The relationship between the Crusader states and the Byzantine Empire was often strained, and Raymond found himself in the midst of these tensions. He had to carefully navigate the complex political landscape, balancing the interests of his county with the demands of the Byzantine Emperor. This period was marked by diplomatic maneuvers, occasional military confrontations, and the delicate task of maintaining an uneasy peace between the two powers.\n\n***defense against muslim forces***  \nRaymond III's reign was also defined by the ongoing struggle against Muslim forces in the region. He was a key figure in the defense of the Crusader states against invasions and raids launched by various Muslim rulers. His military campaigns and strategic alliances were crucial in holding back the advance of Muslim armies and preserving the territorial integrity of the Crusader states. These efforts not only ensured the survival of Tripoli but also bolstered the broader Crusader presence in the Levant.\n\n****\n\nThis summary highlights key aspects of Raymond III's life and reign, emphasizing his early life, reign as Count of Tripoli, contributions and legacy, conflicts with the Byzantine Empire, and defense against Muslim forces. His leadership and strategic decisions were pivotal in shaping the history of the Crusader states during a turbulent period.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -2.5707879066467285}, {"token": "*", "logprob": -2.5210065841674805}, {"token": "early", "logprob": -5.8207621574401855}, {"token": " life", "logprob": -0.15869861841201782}, {"token": "***", "logprob": -0.493411660194397}, {"token": "  ", "logprob": -1.1263623237609863}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -1.811964830267243e-05}, {"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.5780264139175415}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.0015657796757295728}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0014042527182027698}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.17778344452381134}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.04511331021785736}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.649054244509898e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00011860620725201443}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -5.411955135